[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (5 issue(s)) — The diff correctly applies the prescribed minimal fix: adding live_preview: { host, management_token, enable } to the Contentstack Stack options object, plus destructuring the two new env vars (CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST). This is the correct root cause — the SDK-level configuration that enables the Contentstack Live Preview service. The change is concise (7 lines) and matches the prescribed fix exactly. However, there are blockers: (1) No unit tests were added for the new live_preview configuration, violating the test coverage requirement; (2) No error/warning is logged when the preview token is missing, failing the 'clear error or unavailable state' acceptance criterion; (3) The ContentstackContext still uses useMemo with no livePreview callback registration, so the React tree cannot reactively update when a CMS editor changes a field — acceptance criteria 2 and 5 are unmet. Major: the new env vars are not documented in .env.local.sample. The fix addresses the correct root cause and is minimal, but the missing tests, missing error state for unavailable preview, and missing reactive context layer are blockers.

