[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (5 issue(s)) — The implementation adds only 7 lines to src/services/contentstack.ts — the live_preview config block in the Stack options. This partially addresses the second prescribed fix (SDK-level config) but completely omits the first prescribed fix (ContentstackProvider changes). The provider still uses useMemo to freeze content at build-time, no useState/useEffect or live preview callback registration exists, no includeDraft field was added to any interface, no page-level preview propagation exists, and zero unit tests were added. The SDK-level config alone cannot deliver live preview: without a React-side listener that calls setContent on preview events, the context never updates, and without includeDraft propagation through the service layer, draft content can never be fetched. Every acceptance criterion related to real-time draft content rendering (criteria 1, 3, 5) is unmet. Criteria 2, 4, and 6 are technically satisfied by accident (no preview = published content shown), but the implementation does not actively handle them. Verdict: changes_requested with 4 blockers and 1 major issue.

